1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,667
<i>Five minutes never feels like much.</i>

2
00:00:08,667 --> 00:00:11,167
MIA: Story time?

3
00:00:11,233 --> 00:00:14,667
DAD: Five minutes.

4
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:24,600
[clock ticking]

5
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:34,267
DAD (thinking): <i>Oh.</i>

6
00:01:00,533 --> 00:01:03,000
MIA: Story time?

7
00:01:03,133 --> 00:01:06,133
DAD: After this one.

8
00:01:16,333 --> 00:01:19,533
MIA (quietly): Story time?

9
00:01:19,667 --> 00:01:22,733
DAD: Tomorrow, okay?

10
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,667
[Mia walks past without a word]

11
00:02:05,167 --> 00:02:09,667
DAD (thinking): <i>Is that how she sees me?</i>

12
00:02:14,733 --> 00:02:17,167
[phone buzzes]
WEEKLY REPORT — Daily average: 4h 12m

13
00:02:17,333 --> 00:02:24,000
DAD (thinking): <i>Four hours. Every day.</i>

14
00:02:27,333 --> 00:02:36,200
“It is not that we have a short time to live,
but that we waste a lot of it.” — Seneca

15
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:48,500
[alarm] 20:00 — PHONE BOX

16
00:03:00,267 --> 00:03:01,433
[knocking]

17
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:04,000
DAD: Story time?

18
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:17,933
[phone buzzing in the box]

19
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,667
TEMPTATION: Could be important.

20
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,167
TEMPTATION: Just check.

21
00:03:23,333 --> 00:03:25,667
MIA (off-screen): Daddy! Page 12!

22
00:03:26,167 --> 00:03:28,833
DAD: It can wait.

23
00:03:42,333 --> 00:03:51,200
“How we spend our days is, of course,
how we spend our lives.” — Annie Dillard

24
00:03:59,133 --> 00:04:01,333
[clock strikes eight]

25
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:10,167
MIA: Story time.

26
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:13,333
DAD: Story time.

27
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:20,667
MIA: Again!

28
00:04:20,933 --> 00:04:23,500
DAD: Again.

29
00:04:24,333 --> 00:04:27,000
[crickets]

30
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,700
<i>They won’t remember what you scrolled.</i>

31
00:04:37,733 --> 00:04:43,200
<i>They won’t remember what you scrolled.
They’ll remember you.</i>

32
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:53,667
SCROLL
<i>Look up. They’re growing.</i>

